h (a) that the 275\u219219 and 19\u21921707 events lie inside [44240, 82639], (b) that they are correctly ordered in time, or (c) that the gap between them is \u2264 600 units. Since each relay edge fired only once, the ordering/latency test is decisive and unverifiable here.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_2025d7ec\",\n  \"decision\": \"insufficient\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"cascade\",\n  \"entities\": [275, 19, 1707],\n  \"window\": [44240, 82639],\n  \"confidence\": 0.7,\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_03\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_04\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_06\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_08\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_10\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_11\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_12\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_07\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_09\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_13\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_01\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"}\n  ],\n  \"narrative\": \"The only candidate route from 275 to 1707 is the two-hop path through hub node 19, each leg occurring exactly once. Node 19 is a top-10 hub (273 events, 229 partners, 884 triangles), so the ignore-time connection is well explained by hub connectivity alone. All available tools aggregate over the full horizon and expose no timestamps, so I cannot confirm the two relay events fall inside [44240, 82639], are correctly ordered, or are separated by at most 600 time units. Evidence is therefore insufficient to affirm a genuine time-respecting cascade (and insufficient to firmly rule one out).\"\n}\n```", "total_input_tokens": 23564, "total_output_tokens": 4348, "total_tokens": 27912, "total_latency_ms": 62477, "llm_calls": 6, "schema_repairs": 0, "status": "success", "e